# CourtListener API Token (OPTIONAL but strongly recommended)
#
# Without a token the scraper still works: it enumerates via the public search
# API and extracts text from stored PDFs on storage.courtlistener.com. That
# covers roughly 75-80% of opinions filed from 1950 onward.
#
# With a token the scraper also reads the Opinions API (plain_text /
# html_with_citations / xml_harvard), which is the ONLY way to reach the
# pre-1950 corpus (~24K opinions for CA2+CA9 alone) — those clusters have no
# stored file at all.
#
# A token also raises the rate limit to 5,000 queries/hour.
#
# Get one at: https://www.courtlistener.com/sign-in/ (free account, then copy
# the API token from your profile).
COURTLISTENER_API_TOKEN=
